			"id": "101",
			"headline": "Man Invents Time Machine To Procrastinate Better, Gets Stuck In 47 Different Mondays",
			"summary": "The 'Later Lens' allows users to experience the same Monday over and over, perfect for avoiding responsibilities.",
			"fullBody": "Chronic procrastinator Gary Tomorrow has invented the 'Later Lens,' a time machine specifically designed to help people procrastinate more effectively. The device allows users to travel forward in time to 'later' so they can do things 'eventually.' However, Gary accidentally got stuck experiencing 47 consecutive Mondays, each time telling himself 'I'll start being productive next Monday.' Scientists who studied the device said, 'It's technically time travel, but it's also deeply sad.' Gary has since become the first person to file a restraining order against himself, saying 'I can't keep running into me in the hallway saying I'll get to it later.' The Later Lens is now available for pre-order, with a warning label that reads 'Side effects may include eternal procrastination and existential dread.'",
			"category": "tech",
			"imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-09/101.jpg",
			"imagePrompt": "Man with multiple versions of himself all saying TOMORROW, calendar showing Monday 47 times, time machine in background, comic illustration, flat design, purple and blue colors",
			"publishedAt": "1 hr ago",
