			"id": "105",
			"headline": "New App 'Replace My Boss' Lets AI Act As Your Boss So You Can Practice Standing Up To Authority",
			"summary": "The 'Boss Simulator Pro' creates AI bosses that yell about deadlines, allowing you to practice mutiny safely.",
			"fullBody": "Corporate rebellion training startup Mutiny Tech has released 'Boss Simulator Pro,' an app that creates AI bosses for you to practice standing up to. The app uses customization options to create bosses that match your real boss's personality, complete with appropriate levels of yelling, passive aggression, and unreasonable deadlines. Users can practice responses like 'Actually, I have a life outside of work' and 'My mental health matters more than this deadline' in a safe environment. One user said, 'I practiced telling my AI boss 'No' for 47 hours, and when my real boss asked me to work overtime, I said 'No' and it worked. I've never felt more powerful.' The app has a 94% success rate in 'making people feel empowered' and a 47% success rate in 'getting people fired for practicing on real bosses.'",
