			"headline": "New Dating App Uses AI To Write Your Messages, Results In 47% More Dates But 0% Authenticity",
			"summary": "The 'LoveBot' creates perfect messages that get responses but lead to conversations about weather for 47 hours.",
			"fullBody": "LazyLove Technologies has released a dating app called 'LoveBot' that uses AI to write all your messages for you. The AI analyzes potential matches and sends perfectly crafted opening lines, flirty responses, and romantic compliments. One user said, 'I got 47 dates in a month using LoveBot, but every conversation started with \"So, the weather, right?\" because the AI was playing it safe.' Another user said, 'I went on a date with someone and realized I had no idea how to talk to them without the AI, so I just kept saying \"like\" and \"um\" until they thought I was having a stroke.' The app has a feature where you can 'borrow your AI's confidence' for in-person conversations, but users report that it feels 'like being possessed by a more charming version of yourself.'",
