			"id": "108",
			"headline": "Man Programs Smart Fridge To Only Open When He Exercises, Accidentally Loses 30 Pounds",
			"summary": "The 'FitFridge' requires 30 squats before dispensing cheese, and users report never wanting cheese more in their lives.",
			"fullBody": "Fitness enthusiast Mike NoSnacks has programmed his smart fridge to require exercise before opening. The 'FitFridge' uses a camera and AI to detect exercise movements, requiring 30 squats before the door will unlock. 'It's basically a very expensive form of torture,' Mike said, 'but I lost 30 pounds in 3 months, so I can't complain.' The system also includes 'emotional eating prevention mode,' which requires you to tell the fridge why you're really sad before it opens for midnight snacks. One user said, 'I stood in front of my FitFridge at 2 AM, crying, saying \"I'm sad because I ate all my feelings and now I have no feelings left to eat,\" and the fridge finally opened. It felt like therapy.' The FitFridge has been credited with solving America's obesity crisis and also creating America's new fitness obsession.",
