			"headline": "Virtual Reality Game Lets You Experience Your Ex's Life After They Left You",
			"summary": "'Regret Simulator VR' allows users to see their ex thriving while they sit in their parents' basement eating cereal.",
			"fullBody": "Emotional masochism has reached new heights with the release of 'Regret Simulator VR,' a virtual reality game that lets you experience exactly how your ex is doing after the breakup. The game uses AI to generate realistic scenarios of your ex thriving in life while you presumably sit in your parents' basement eating cereal. Features include 'Watch Your Ex Get Promoted While You're Still Unemployed,' 'See Your Ex Go On Vacation While You Go On Reddit,' and 'Experience Your Ex's New Relationship While You Experience A Staring Contest With Your Wall.' One user said, 'I played for 47 minutes and now I'm both crying and somehow motivated to improve my life, which I think was the point, but I'm still mad about it.' The game has a 4.9-star rating with reviews like 'This destroyed me, but I also needed this.'",
