			"headline": "Company Creates 'Meeting Calculator' That Shows How Much Of Your Life You've Lost To Meetings",
			"summary": "The 'TimeIsMoney' app calculates you've spent 47 years in meetings and suggests legal action against your employer.",
			"fullBody": "TimeIsMoney Analytics has created a meeting calculator that tracks how much of your life you've spent in meetings and delivers brutal honesty about your work-life balance. The app integrates with your calendar and calculates your total meeting hours, displaying results like 'You have spent 47 years in meetings, which is longer than the average human lifespan' and 'You've sat in 12,000 meetings that could have been emails.' One user reported that after running the calculation, they received a suggestion that read 'Based on our analysis, we recommend suing your employer for theft of life.' The app also offers a 'Meeting Mortality Risk' score that tells you how much of your finite time on Earth has been spent discussing 'synergy' and 'low-hanging fruit.' The company is now offering a premium version that sends resignation letter templates.",
