			"headline": "New App 'Replace My Friends' Uses AI To Attend Social Events So You Don't Have To",
			"summary": "The 'SocialAvoid' bot shows up to parties, makes small talk, and reports back everything that happened without you.",
			"fullBody": "Anti-social networking startup StayHome Tech has released 'SocialAvoid,' an app that uses AI avatars to attend social events on your behalf. The AI attends parties, weddings, and work happy hours, makes appropriate small talk, and sends you detailed reports about what happened. One user said, 'The AI went to my friend's birthday party and told me \"They mentioned you 47 times and only 12 were positive. Also, someone asked if you were still alive.\" It was incredibly helpful and also incredibly devastating.' The AI can mimic your personality, laugh at the right jokes, and even eat food on your behalf. However, the company warns that 'using the AI too frequently may result in friends forgetting who you are, which may actually be the goal.' The app has been downloaded 5 million times, primarily by introverts and people with social anxiety.",
