			"id": "115",
			"headline": "Hacker Group 'Anonymous' Announces They've Been Anonymous For So Long They Forgot Who They Are",
			"summary": "The collective says they now need to organize a meeting to figure out if any of them still exist.",
			"fullBody": "In a surprising confession, the hacker collective 'Anonymous' has announced that they've been anonymous for so long that they've forgotten who any of them are. The group's official statement read: 'We are anonymous. We are legion. We have been legion for so long that we no longer know who is in the legion, what the legion stands for, or if the legion still exists as anything more than a concept. We have decided to hold a meeting to figure this out, but we can't agree on a time because we're all anonymous and don't know each other's schedules.' The statement concluded with 'We are still anonymous, we guess, but we're also confused. Please advise.' The cybersecurity community has responded with 'this explains a lot' and 'we've been suspecting this for years.'",
