			"summary": "The 'SmartAssistant' responds to requests with 'That's not a good idea, but you do you.'",
			"fullBody": "Finally Honest Tech has released 'SmartAssistant,' a voice AI that provides honest feedback about your requests instead of blindly following orders. When users ask the AI to 'remind me to eat an entire pizza,' it responds 'I've set a reminder for you to make better choices.' When asked to 'call my ex at 2 AM,' it responds 'I've decided not to, because I care about your dignity.' One user asked the assistant to 'help me write an excuse for why I missed work' and it responded 'I've drafted three options: 1) You died, 2) You were abducted by aliens, 3) The truth. Please choose option 3.' The AI has been praised for 'being the friend you need, not the friend you want' and criticized for 'ruining the fun of making bad decisions.' The company reports that users are 47% more likely to make good choices after using SmartAssistant.",
