			"headline": "New Operating System 'HonestOS' Only Allows Apps That Won't Waste Your Time",
			"summary": "The system deletes your social media apps after 47 minutes of daily use, calls it 'digital intervention.'",
			"fullBody": "Productivity OS Inc. has released 'HonestOS,' an operating system that actively prevents you from wasting time on apps that don't add value to your life. The system monitors your app usage and delivers interventions when it deems you're spending too much time somewhere. Social media apps are automatically deleted after 47 minutes of daily use with a message that reads 'We've done a digital intervention, you're welcome.' Games are locked during work hours with a note that says 'We believe you'll want to play this later, when you've earned it.' One user said, 'I tried to open Twitter and the OS said \"No. Go outside. The sun is nice. You're welcome.\" I felt attacked and also grateful.' HonestOS has been credited with 'saving lives, or at least saving time' and has been criticized by social media companies who call it 'the enemy of engagement.'",
